														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2727342">
									

<p>It just occurred to me that part of my emotional response to this ongoing story is sheer outrage. Maine has, for some unknowable reason, received powers almost godlike. And this petty, sordid assholery is what he does with them? Not only is he evil, his evil is as dull and stupid as real life evil. He lacks even the imagination and creativity to mimic fictional evil.</p>
<p>You (the author) created a villain who could exist in real life - a Dolores Umbridge, not a Voldemort. Maybe that's why I despise him so enthusiastically. Well done! This entire tale has kept my attention from start to finish.</p>
<p>And I SO did not see the twist coming.</p>

							</div>

								
					
